    <string name="help">Help and feedback</string>
    <string name="help_text">• Counting stopped? Open Settings → the Fix card, or More → Permissions, and turn everything green.\n\n• Accessibility switch greyed out? Open App info for Rokoreels, tap ⋮ → Allow restricted settings, then try again.\n\n• The first reel you open isn\'t counted until you swipe to the next one.\n\n• An app stopped being counted after an update? It renamed its reels screen; tell us which app and version.</string>
    <string name="privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_sub">What you watch never leaves your phone</string>
    <string name="privacy_text">Rokoreels uses Android\'s Accessibility service to count your reels and time, and to close apps when it\'s time to stop. It sees which app is open and for how long, when a new reel starts, and labels like \"Sponsored\" so ads don\'t count. It shows Iris over the apps you picked. It closes Reels, or the whole app, when you reach a limit or focus hours, by pressing Back or Home for you, also for Block Reels, app timers and your daily time limit. It never reads your messages or passwords, never types for you or taps inside your apps, and what\'s on your screen never leaves your phone. Counts and settings are kept in the app\'s private storage on this phone.\n\nAnonymous usage stats (Google Analytics for Firebase): which setup steps you finish, when a limit, pause or block screen happens, and a daily total of reels per app. No names, emails or advertising ID. Turn it off in More → Share anonymous usage stats.\n\nYou sign in with Google when you set up Rokoreels. It links only your name and email to an account; your counts and settings stay on this phone.</string>
    <string name="share_stats">Share anonymous usage stats</string>
    <string name="share_stats_sub">Daily reel totals and which screens you use. No names or what you watch.</string>
    <string name="about">About Rokoreels</string>
    <string name="about_text">Rokoreels %1$s\n\nCounts every reel and helps you stop when you mean to.\n\nFonts: Bricolage Grotesque and Inter, both under the SIL Open Font License.</string>

