    <string name="full_title">About Android\'s \"full control\" message</string>
    <string name="full_text">Android shows the same message for every app that uses Accessibility, including screen readers. Here\'s what each line means for Rokoreels.</string>
    <string name="full_q1">\"View and control screen\"</string>
    <string name="full_a1">Rokoreels checks which app is open and for how long, whether a new reel appeared, and looks for labels like \"Sponsored\" or \"Ad\" so ads aren\'t counted. It also shows Iris on top of the apps you picked. It never reads your messages or passwords.</string>
    <string name="full_q2">\"View and perform actions\"</string>
    <string name="full_a2">Rokoreels notices your swipe. It presses Back or Home to close Reels or the app when you reach your daily limit, during focus hours, when you use Block Reels, or when an app timer or your daily time limit runs out. It never types for you or taps inside your apps.</string>
    <string name="got_it">Got it</string>
    <string name="grey_title">If the switch is greyed out</string>
    <string name="grey_text">Android blocks Accessibility for apps installed outside the Play Store until you allow it once.</string>
    <string name="grey_s1">Open <b>App info</b> for Rokoreels</string>
    <string name="grey_s2">Tap <b>⋮</b> in the top corner</string>
